{"lines":[{"c":1,"t":"Reading","y":0.097988484377950824,"x":0.79591825679473094,"w":0.078925832112630046,"h":0.015179330805586533},{"c":1,"x":0.090481853257156034,"h":0.018309392693185988,"w":0.75113235473632811,"t":"more fundamental than whether the visitor is a little girl or three siblings, or the animal is a tiger","y":0.14086766228499747},{"y":0.158421672383257,"x":0.092592592701899623,"w":0.13786008199055991,"h":0.01308995562532056,"c":1,"t":"instead of a wolf."},{"y":0.19186046497041809,"w":0.75720163981119781,"t":"However, Tehrani found no significant difference in the rate of evolution of incidents compared","h":0.016031172025610885,"c":1,"x":0.09053498246065611},{"w":0.77572016398111976,"x":0.092592592792377484,"t":"with that of characters.ạẠạiCertain episodes are very stable because they are crucial to the story, but","h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"y":0.20784883706259738},{"c":1,"w":0.78422866821289072,"x":0.090394214379245927,"h":0.021928923149692969,"t":"there are lots of other details that can evolve quite freely,' he says. Neither did his analysis support","y":0.22100717150584315},{"h":0.016195524146054296,"x":0.090534981605152706,"c":1,"t":"the theory that the central section of a story is the most conserved part. He found no significant","y":0.2411660777471607,"w":0.76337448120117191},{"y":0.25872093008635955,"w":0.66255142211914053,"c":1,"x":0.092592601593776983,"t":"difference in the flexibility of events there compared with the beginning or the end.","h":0.016014052504504717},{"w":0.77169937133789068,"h":0.018665080076112006,"c":1,"t":"But the really big surprise came when he looked at the cautionary elements of the story. 'Studies","y":0.29055279051865712,"x":0.092550332926003787},{"t":"on hunter-gatherer folk tales suggest that these narratives include really important information","x":0.092592609724131025,"y":0.30668604669851196,"h":0.01751890002768508,"c":1,"w":0.75308639526367194},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.74279836018880208,"t":"about the environment and the possible dangers that may be faced there - stuff that's relevant","y":0.3241279068305134,"c":1,"x":0.090534976182633883},{"w":0.75102879842122394,"c":1,"t":"to survival,' he says. Yet in his analysis such elements were just as flexible as seemingly trivial","y":0.34156976729581856,"x":0.090534983410166303,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"t":"details. What, then, is important enough to be reproduced from generation to generation?","c":1,"x":0.090534985185647371,"y":0.357479387497043,"h":0.01752061192363108,"w":0.71399175008138016},{"y":0.39058381408395826,"h":0.018091111357276701,"x":0.09252280551650624,"w":0.7779040018717448,"c":1,"t":"The answer, it would appear, is fear - blood-thirsty and gruesome aspects of the story, such as the"},{"h":0.015996932421752708,"c":1,"t":"eating of the grandmother by the wolf, turned out to be the best preserved of all. Why are these","x":0.090534990628922285,"w":0.75925923665364592,"y":0.40842167237059646},{"h":0.01857281405175959,"t":"details retained by generations of storytellers, when other features are not? Tehrani has an idea:","w":0.75938761393229171,"y":0.4242036357787673,"x":0.092523508410486288,"c":1},{"t":"'In an oral context, a story won't survive because of one great teller. It also needs to be interesting","w":0.78189300537109374,"y":0.44040697658509076,"h":0.017484660423826903,"c":1,"x":0.092592591858997556},{"y":0.45784883706228063,"h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.73456792195638021,"x":0.090534968929088203,"c":1,"t":"when it's told by someone who's not necessarily a great storyteller? Maybe being swallowed"},{"h":0.016014052504504717,"t":"whole by a wolf, then cut out of its stomach alive is so gripping that it helps the story remain","y":0.47526501740432336,"x":0.092592581186610415,"w":0.74074076334635419,"c":1},{"w":0.3086419677734375,"c":1,"x":0.090534983100552746,"h":0.016195524146054185,"t":"popular, no matter how badly it's told.","y":0.49263839809617127},{"x":0.090534983389457008,"y":0.52470930216613476,"c":1,"h":0.017441860778592999,"w":0.75102879842122394,"t":"Jack Zipes at the University of Minnesota, Minneapolis, is unconvinced by Tehrani's views on"},{"y":0.54063604246351571,"w":0.7613168334960938,"x":0.090535003005039513,"t":"fairy tales. 'Even if they're gruesome, they won't stick unless they matter, he says. He believes","c":1,"h":0.017503491840879293},{"y":0.55668604669851196,"h":0.01751890002768508,"t":"the perennial theme of women as victims in stories like Little Red Riding Hood explains why they","x":0.090534977355605409,"w":0.78189300537109374,"c":1},{"t":"continue to feel relevant. But Tehrani points out that although this is often the case in Western","h":0.015996932421752819,"x":0.092592580241819461,"y":0.57558139520268548,"c":1,"w":0.74691360473632806},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"y":0.59156976723156551,"w":0.75925923665364581,"t":"versions, it is not always true elsewhere. In Chinese and Japanese versions, often known as The","x":0.092592601349102965},{"y":0.60895170801972465,"w":0.73868311564127609,"x":0.092592598451503624,"t":"Tiger Grandmother, the villain is a woman, and in both Iran and Nigeria, the victim is a boy.","c":1,"h":0.017501780506578912},{"t":"Mathias Clasen at Aarhus University in Denmark isn't surprised by Tehrani's findings.Habits","y":0.64244186033247108,"x":0.092592596569844171,"c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074,"w":0.75102879842122394},{"y":0.6584216723705808,"t":"and morals change, but the things that scare us, and the fact that we seek out entertainment that's","h":0.015996932421752819,"c":1,"w":0.77366256713867188,"x":0.090534971459883498},{"y":0.67427153960871367,"x":0.094591847859002293,"c":1,"t":"designed to scare us - those are constant,' he says. Clasen believes that scary stories teach us what","w":0.78198786417643218,"h":0.017100043235032891},{"w":0.75308639526367194,"h":0.017503492402524912,"c":1,"t":"it feels like to be afraid without having to experience real danger, and so build up resistance to","y":0.69186046495690601,"x":0.090534991555437996},{"y":0.7093023254466293,"x":0.094650205742342688,"h":0.013081395583944611,"t":"negative emotions.","w":0.15226337432861325,"c":1},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.84979423878628757,"c":1,"t":"67","w":0.024691357612609877,"y":0.91715116260773688},{"t":"PANDOL","y":0.96220930221989898,"c":0.30000001192092896,"x":0.030864197418265224,"h":0.0072674419910804255,"w":0.030864197413126626}],"w":2400,"h":3395}